cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "budgetroll: hierarchical margin and budget rollup with explicit combination rules"
abstract: >-
  Reads a hierarchical engineering budget from YAML - mass, power, data
  volume or the log-domain terms of a link budget - with a per-item
  contingency keyed to a declared maturity policy, a declared combination
  rule at every node, and a declared leaf-to-leaf correlation structure. It
  keeps deterministic contingency and random uncertainty strictly apart,
  summing the first and propagating the second by the law of propagation of
  uncertainty; it reports the linear, root-sum-square, declared-hierarchy and
  exact correlated combinations side by side at every node; and it checks the
  independence assumption that root-sum-square requires against the declared
  correlations, reporting ten named findings. Deterministic, with no learned
  component. Educational-grade (validation level 1): not flight-qualified, not
  certified, not approved for operational aerospace use, and it discharges no
  engineering obligation.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-16"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Acharya
    given-names: Om
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/budgetroll"
keywords:
  - margin
  - budget
  - mass budget
  - power budget
  - link budget
  - uncertainty propagation
  - systems engineering
  - aerospace
references:
  - type: report
    title: >-
      JCGM 100:2008, Evaluation of measurement data - Guide to the expression
      of uncertainty in measurement
    institution:
      name: "Joint Committee for Guides in Metrology, BIPM"
    year: 2008
    notes: >-
      Section 5.1.2, the law of propagation of uncertainty for uncorrelated
      inputs, and section 5.2.2, the correlated case. These are the two
      equations the aggregation in this package implements.
  - type: article
    title: "A Note on a Simple Transmission Formula"
    authors:
      - family-names: Friis
        given-names: "Harald T."
    journal: "Proceedings of the I.R.E."
    volume: 34
    issue: 5
    start: 254
    end: 256
    year: 1946
    notes: >-
      The free-space transmission formula reproduced in
      validation/validate_link_budget.py.
  - type: book
    title: "Space Mission Analysis and Design"
    editors:
      - family-names: Wertz
        given-names: "James R."
      - family-names: Larson
        given-names: "Wiley J."
    edition: "3rd"
    publisher:
      name: "Microcosm Press and Kluwer Academic Publishers"
    year: 1999
    notes: >-
      Chapter 13, Communications Architecture, cited by chapter title for the
      decibel form of the link equation. No equation number and no page number
      is quoted anywhere in this repository, because the edition was not
      available in the container the validation was run in; every constant the
      equation uses is instead reproduced from first principles in
      validation/validate_link_budget.py.
  - type: standard
    title: "ANSI/AIAA S-120A-2015, Mass Properties Control for Space Systems"
    institution:
      name: "American Institute of Aeronautics and Astronautics"
    year: 2015
    notes: >-
      Cited as the published source of maturity-keyed mass growth allowance
      practice. No table from it is reproduced in this repository; the margin
      policies in the example cases are declared by the author of those files.
  - type: report
    title: "NASA Systems Engineering Handbook"
    number: "NASA/SP-2016-6105 Rev 2"
    institution:
      name: "National Aeronautics and Space Administration"
    year: 2016
    notes: >-
      Cited as the published source of margin and contingency practice,
      section 6.5. No table from it is reproduced here.
